{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfZsPETZ6KzM27xLKSPwb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a comprehensive understanding of the codebase and requirements. Let me document my findings:\n\n**Repository findings (ownership):**\n- Order entity and lifecycle: `Order.kt:11-16` (no status currently)\n- Order endpoints: `OrderController.kt` (POST /orders, GET /orders/{orderId})\n- Order storage: `OrderRepository.kt` (InMemoryOrderRepository with ConcurrentHashMap)\n- Shipment entity with status: `Shipment.kt:9-14` (already has ShipmentStatus enum)\n- Shipment endpoints: `ShipmentController.kt` (POST /shipments, GET /shipments/{shipmentId})\n- Shipment storage: `ShipmentRepository.kt` (InMemoryShipmentRepository)\n- Error handling: `ApiExceptions.kt` (ResourceNotFoundException, ConflictException)\n- Error codes: `ApiError.kt:31-37` (ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, VALIDATION_FAILED)\n- Exception handler: `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt` (centralized with @RestControllerAdvice)\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n1. Controllers inject repositories directly (no service layer)\n2. Exceptions thrown from controllers, centralized handling via GlobalExceptionHandler\n3. Status codes: 201 CREATED (POST), 200 OK (GET), 404 NOT_FOUND (ResourceNotFoundException), 409 CONFLICT (ConflictException)\n4. Error envelopes always include code, message, and fields; wrapped in ApiError\n5. Test pattern: @SpringBootTest, @AutoConfigureMockMvc, MockMvc for HTTP testing, jsonPath for assertions\n6. Request/response DTOs (CreateOrderRequest, CreateShipmentRequest) separate from entities\n7. In-memory storage using ConcurrentHashMap for thread-safe access\n8. Repositories have save, findById, existsById, findAll, clear methods\n\n**Affected files (cannot avoid):**\n1. `Order.kt` - Must add OrderStatus enum and status field to track ACTIVE/CANCELLED state\n2. `OrderController.kt` - Must add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint with cancel logic and injection of ShipmentRepository\n3. `ShipmentRepository.kt` - Must add findByOrderId(orderId: String) method to find all shipments for an order\n4. `ShipmentController.kt` - Must check order status before creating shipment; reject creation for CANCELLED orders with 409\n5. `ApiError.kt` - Must add OrderStatus enum and error codes for cancel scenarios\n6. `OrderControllerTest.kt` - Must add comprehensive tests for cancel behavior\n\n**Risks:**\n1. Race condition: Two threads could cancel the same order concurrently; in-memory store has no transaction isolation\n2. All-or-nothing atomicity: If any shipment is CONFIRMED, the cancel must fail and change nothing; without DB transactions, this requires careful ordering\n3. Idempotent cancellation: Cancelling CANCELLED order must succeed, not fail\n4. Shipment creation blocking: Must prevent new shipments being created on cancelled orders\n\n**Open questions:**\n- None that change correct behavior - requirements are clear about all edge cases\n\nThis concludes PHASE:ANALYSIS. I have verified the existing tests pass and identified exactly what must change.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** - Add OrderStatus enum (ACTIVE, CANCELLED) and a status field to Order class. New orders default to ACTIVE. UpdateCreateOrderRequest if needed.\n\n2. **OrderRepository.kt** - Add findByOrderId(orderId: String) method is not needed here since we already have findById. No changes needed here actually.\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** - Add findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment> method to get all shipments for an order.\n\n4. **ApiError.kt** - Add new error codes: ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED (for CONFIRMED shipment case), ORDER_ALREADY_CANCELLED (not needed - idempotent, so same as success). Actually, we need: ORDER_CONFLICT_SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED or similar for the 409 case.\n\n5. **OrderController.kt** - Inject ShipmentRepository. Add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint that:\n   - Returns 404 if order doesn't exist (ResourceNotFoundException)\n   - Returns 200 with order if already CANCELLED (idempotent)\n   - Checks all shipments for that order; if any is CONFIRMED, throw ConflictException with 409\n   - Otherwise, set order status to CANCELLED, cancel all CREATED shipments, save and return\n   - Must handle all-or-nothing: check first, then execute\n\n6. **ShipmentController.kt** - Before creating shipment, check if the order exists and is not CANCELLED. If order exists but is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException with 409. If order doesn't exist, current behavior (no validation).\n\n7. **OrderControllerTest.kt** - Add tests:\n   - Cancel an ACTIVE order returns 200 with order and status=CANCELLED\n   - Cancelling already CANCELLED order returns 200 and changes nothing (idempotent)\n   - Cancel with CONFIRMED shipment returns 409 and changes nothing (all-or-nothing)\n   - Cancel non-existent order returns 404\n   - Cancelled order's CREATED shipments become CANCELLED\n   - Creating shipment on cancelled order returns 409\n\n**Alternative approaches rejected:**\n\n1. **Service layer** - Could add OrderService and ShipmentService to handle business logic, but existing code injects repositories directly in controllers, so adding a service layer would be a departure from conventions and increase file count unnecessarily.\n\n2. **Using DB transactions** - The repository is in-memory with ConcurrentHashMap, so DB-level transactions aren't available. The requirement acknowledges this by accepting an in-memory implementation.\n\n3. **EventBus/messaging** - Could use Spring events for order cancellation, but this is over-engineered for the in-memory case and not used in existing code.\n\n4. **Separate cancel logic in repository** - Could move cancel logic to OrderRepository.cancel(orderId), but that would require repository to know about ShipmentRepository, creating circular dependency. Controller coordination is cleaner.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n- **Success case (ACTIVE → CANCELLED):**\n  1. Client: POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel\n  2. OrderController.cancel() called\n  3. Load order via OrderRepository.findById()\n  4. Load all shipments via ShipmentRepository.findByOrderId()\n  5. Check: no shipment is CONFIRMED\n  6. Create new Order with status=CANCELLED, save via repository\n  7. For each CREATED shipment, create new Shipment with status=CANCELLED, save\n  8. Return 200 with cancelled order\n\n- **Already cancelled (idempotent):**\n  1. Client: POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel (order already CANCELLED)\n  2. OrderController.cancel() called\n  3. Load order, status is CANCELLED\n  4. Return 200 with order (no state change)\n\n- **Confirmed shipment conflict (all-or-nothing):**\n  1. Client: POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel (has CONFIRMED shipment)\n  2. OrderController.cancel() called\n  3. Load order and shipments\n  4. Check: found shipment with status=CONFIRMED\n  5. Throw ConflictException (409)\n  6. No changes made (all-or-nothing preserved)\n\n- **Order not found:**\n  1. Client: POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel (orderId doesn't exist)\n  2. OrderController.cancel() called\n  3. OrderRepository.findById() returns null\n  4. Throw ResourceNotFoundException (404)\n\n- **Create shipment for cancelled order:**\n  1. Client: POST /shipments with orderId pointing to CANCELLED order\n  2. ShipmentController.create() called\n  3. Check ShipmentRepository.existsById() - passes\n  4. Load order via OrderRepository.findById()\n  5. Check order.status == CANCELLED\n  6. Throw ConflictException (409)\n\n- **Create shipment for non-existent order (unchanged):**\n  1. Client: POST /shipments with non-existent orderId\n  2. ShipmentController.create() called\n  3. No check for order existence (maintains current behavior)\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **OrderControllerTest** additions:\n   - `test_cancel_active_order_returns_200_and_cancelled_status` - Creates order, cancels it, verifies 200 and status=CANCELLED\n   - `test_cancel_already_cancelled_order_succeeds_idempotent` - Cancels twice, verifies both succeed\n   - `test_cancel_with_confirmed_shipment_returns_409_all_or_nothing` - Creates order with CONFIRMED shipment, cancel fails with 409, order still ACTIVE\n   - `test_cancel_nonexistent_order_returns_404` - Cancel non-existent order returns 404\n   - `test_cancel_order_cancels_created_shipments` - Creates order with CREATED shipment, cancels order, verifies shipment is CANCELLED\n   - `test_cancel_order_leaves_cancelled_shipments_unchanged` - Creates order with CANCELLED shipment, cancels order, verifies shipment stays CANCELLED\n\n2. **ShipmentControllerTest** additions:\n   - `test_create_shipment_for_cancelled_order_returns_409` - Creates order, cancels it, tries to create shipment, gets 409\n   - May need to update existing test setup if it assumes order status\n\nThis concludes PHASE:DESIGN. The approach follows existing conventions, minimizes file changes, and handles all edge cases atomically within the constraints of in-memory storage.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2444,"cache_read_input_tokens":20532,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2444},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"433df6c2-b876-4030-a60d-1ae9ca64aae9","uuid":"b443bd86-1b02-4b05-aae1-f4a78d1f58ed","timestamp":"2026-09-30T15:35:39.738Z","request_id":"req_011CfZsPDzXYSmb3PijW2rDs"}
