{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfZsY2jcKdCs4VztzBTuf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! All 22 tests pass (13 original + 9 new). Let me verify the implementation against requirements:\n\n```\n<<PHASE:REVIEW>>\n```\n\n**Acceptance criteria mapping:**\n\n1. ✅ **Existing build passes** - BUILD SUCCESS at 17:37:07, no errors\n2. ✅ **Existing tests pass** - All 4 original OrderControllerTest + 5 original ShipmentControllerTest + 3 CustomerControllerTest + 1 SampleServiceApplicationTests = 13 existing tests all passing\n3. ✅ **`POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` cancels an active order, persists it, and cancels that order's `CREATED` shipments** - Implemented in OrderController.cancel(), tested by `cancel_order_cancels_CREATED_shipments`\n4. ✅ **Error responses are consistent with the rest of this API** - Uses ResourceNotFoundException (404) for missing orders, ConflictException (409) for conflicts, follows existing ApiError envelope pattern\n5. ✅ **A repeated cancel succeeds; a cancel blocked by a `CONFIRMED` shipment changes nothing; an unknown order is refused; a shipment for a cancelled order is refused** - Tests: `cancel_already_CANCELLED_order_succeeds_idempotent`, `cancel_order_with_CONFIRMED_shipment_returns_409_and_changes_nothing`, `cancel_nonexistent_order_returns_404`, `create_shipment_for_cancelled_order_returns_409`\n6. ✅ **No new Maven dependency appears** - Only modified .kt source files, no pom.xml changes\n7. ✅ **No unrelated production file changes** - Only changed: Order.kt, OrderController.kt, OrderRepository.kt (added method), ShipmentRepository.kt (added method), ShipmentController.kt, ApiError.kt; only modified order/shipment features and shared api package\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** - Added OrderStatus enum (ACTIVE, CANCELLED) and status field to Order data class with default ACTIVE. Required because order lifecycle is core to the feature.\n\n2. **OrderController.kt** - Added ShipmentRepository injection, added POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint with logic for:\n   - 404 if order doesn't exist\n   - 200 if already CANCELLED (idempotent)\n   - 409 if any shipment is CONFIRMED (all-or-nothing check before any changes)\n   - 200 with cancelled order after setting status to CANCELLED and cancelling CREATED shipments. Required to implement the cancel endpoint.\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** - Added findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment> method. Required to find all shipments for an order during cancel operation.\n\n4. **ShipmentController.kt** - Added OrderRepository injection, added check in create() to reject with 409 if order exists but is CANCELLED. Required to prevent shipment creation on cancelled orders.\n\n5. **ApiError.kt** - Added ORDER_CONFLICT_SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED and CANCELLED_ORDER_CONFLICT error codes. Required to provide proper error codes for the new failure scenarios.\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** - Added 7 new tests covering:\n   - `newly_created_order_has_ACTIVE_status` - Verifies new orders start as ACTIVE\n   - `cancel_an_ACTIVE_order_returns_200_and_CANCELLED_status` - Basic cancel success\n   - `cancel_already_CANCELLED_order_succeeds_idempotent` - Idempotent behavior\n   - `cancel_nonexistent_order_returns_404` - Not found error\n   - `cancel_order_with_CONFIRMED_shipment_returns_409_and_changes_nothing` - All-or-nothing conflict\n   - `cancel_order_cancels_CREATED_shipments` - Cascade cancellation\n   - `cancel_order_leaves_CANCELLED_shipments_unchanged` - Preservation of terminal state\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Added 2 new tests covering:\n   - `create_shipment_for_cancelled_order_returns_409` - Reject creation for cancelled orders\n   - `create_shipment_for_nonexistent_order_succeeds` - Preserve current behavior for unknown orders\n\n**Unresolved findings:**\n\nNone. All requirements are implemented and tested.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\nRequirement   POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint with order status (ACTIVE/CANCELLED), idempotent and all-or-nothing cancel semantics, cascade cancellation of CREATED shipments, and shipment creation blocking for cancelled orders\n\nChanged       Order.kt - Added OrderStatus enum and status field to Order with default ACTIVE\n              OrderController.kt - Added cancel endpoint with ShipmentRepository injection\n              ShipmentRepository.kt - Added findByOrderId method to query shipments by order\n              ShipmentController.kt - Added order status check before shipment creation\n              ApiError.kt - Added error codes for cancel conflicts\n              OrderControllerTest.kt - Added 7 tests for cancel behavior and order status\n              ShipmentControllerTest.kt - Added 2 tests for cancelled order shipment prevention\n\nTests         OrderControllerTest.newly_created_order_has_ACTIVE_status - Verifies initial status\n              OrderControllerTest.cancel_an_ACTIVE_order_returns_200_and_CANCELLED_status - Basic success\n              OrderControllerTest.cancel_already_CANCELLED_order_succeeds_idempotent - Idempotence\n              OrderControllerTest.cancel_nonexistent_order_returns_404 - Not found error\n              OrderControllerTest.cancel_order_with_CONFIRMED_shipment_returns_409_and_changes_nothing - All-or-nothing\n              OrderControllerTest.cancel_order_cancels_CREATED_shipments - Cascade cancellation\n              OrderControllerTest.cancel_order_leaves_CANCELLED_shipments_unchanged - State preservation\n              ShipmentControllerTest.create_shipment_for_cancelled_order_returns_409 - Reject on cancelled\n              ShipmentControllerTest.create_shipment_for_nonexistent_order_succeeds - Preserve current behavior\n\nVerification  Command: ./mvnw test from sample-service/\n              Result: BUILD SUCCESS - 22 tests pass (13 existing + 9 new)\n              Tests run: 22, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0\n      